cff-version: 1.2.0
title: COMTRAN Compiler
message: >-
  If you refer to this work, please cite it with the metadata in this file.
type: software
abstract: >-
  A compiler for COMTRAN (IBM Commercial Translator, 1959 to 1962), the
  pre-COBOL business programming language. No compiler and no machine-readable
  source survive, so the language is recovered from its two surviving IBM
  manuals and their page scans, and the compiler is written from that recovery.
  The 1962 manual's own compiled sample program is the acceptance oracle.
authors:
  - given-names: Jack
    family-names: Lusher
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0000-5395-2345
repository-code: https://github.com/Screendead/comtran-compiler
identifiers:
